{
  /*
   * The project every file in this directory belongs to, Tests/App and
   * Tests/UI aside: exactly ../tsconfig.tests.rest.json, the part of
   * `npm run compile-tests` that type-checks every Common test outside those
   * two (see ../Scripts/compile-tests.js). Its "include" and "exclude" are
   * inherited and resolve against packages/Common, where they are written.
   * Tests/App/tsconfig.json and Tests/UI/tsconfig.json are the other two
   * parts.
   *
   * It exists because TypeScript picks a file's project by the nearest
   * tsconfig.json - editors, and ESLint's typed linting (projectService in
   * eslint.config.js). ../tsconfig.json excludes Tests, so without this file
   * the lookup walked on up to the repository-root tsconfig.json, which has
   * no "include": every Common test was linted, and opened in an editor,
   * inside a program of the whole monorepo.
   *
   * It used to extend ../tsconfig.tests.json, every Common test as one
   * program. Scripts/Lint/LintByProject.js lints each program in an ESLint
   * process of its own, with a 12 GB heap, and on 2026-10-27 that one ran out
   * of it (7,996 files, 916 s; 584 s at 7,910 files the evening before).
   * Measured on its own, the program was most of it: linting 798 of its files
   * peaked at 9.9 GB, 1,776 at 11.3 GB, 3,450 at 12.7 GB. So ESLint gets the
   * three programs compile-tests already checks, each holding only the
   * sources its own tests reach.
   */
  "extends": "../tsconfig.tests.rest.json"
}
